      "dom_id": "question-48722",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14275241/assets/4915dc00f10fa5edc911cf9744e99e662b705898b32f16391805c7733b8f89e5.png)\n\nThe surface area $A$ of the sphere above is increasing. The radius of the sphere is $r.$ Find the rate of change of the surface area of a sphere with respect to its radius.",
      "worked_solution": "The area of the surface area of the sphere is given by  \n\n$$\nA=A(r)=4\\pi {r}^{2}\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $A(r)$ with respect to its radius $r$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}r}(4\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\pi (2r) \\\\  & =8\\pi r.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
